{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975789,"nonce":"eom9BivZRz64Jf8rcTWClUv6Fk8=","title":"No parity row compiles a body that runs once","message":"`--mode jit` is the tiered rung: a body that runs once stays in the interpreter,\nso a lowering bug in a startup-only shape passes every parity row and only appears\nwhen AOT compiles everything. `tools/aot/smoke.sh` is the only check that executes\nsuch bodies compiled, and CI does not run it.\n\nAdd an AOT lane to the test workflow. Until then a fix in the LLVM lowering is\nonly proven by the smoke script. This is the gap that let the null-Dynamic\ndereference class through.","files":null}]}